* A behavioural op-amp written for the CopperScript examples, in the PSpice
* dialect (VALUE, LIMIT, IF, TABLE, I() probes, R_NOISELESS). Its design
* values, which the benches check:
*   open-loop gain      100 dB (1 mS into 100 Mohm)
*   gain-bandwidth      10 MHz (1 mS into 15.915 pF)
*   slew rate           10 V/us (the input stage limited to 159.15 uA)
*   voltage noise       4.99 nV/rtHz, white (a 1.5 kohm thermal resistor)
*   output              10 ohm, 0.3 V from either rail, 30 mA current limit
*   supply current      1.5 mA quiescent plus the output current
* Pins: non-inverting input, inverting input, positive supply, negative
* supply, output.
.SUBCKT BEHAVIOURAL_OPAMP INP INN VCC VEE OUT
.PARAM GM=1M A0=1E5 GBW=10MEG SR=10E6 RSW=0.3 ILIM=30M IQ=1.5M
.PARAM CP={GM/(2*PI*GBW)} IMAX={SR*CP}
* Mid-supply reference.
E_MID MID 0 VALUE={(V(VCC)+V(VEE))/2}
* Input: the noise resistor, common-mode and differential capacitance.
R_EN INP N_INP 1.5K
C_CMP N_INP MID C_UNIT 2P
C_CMN INN MID 2P
C_DIFF N_INP INN 1P
* Transconductance stage, slew limited, into the dominant pole.
G_IN MID N_P VALUE={LIMIT(GM*V(N_INP,INN), -IMAX, IMAX)}
R_P N_P MID R_NOISELESS {A0/GM}
C_P N_P MID {CP}
* Output buffer with swing limits, output resistance and current sense.
E_OUT N_O MID VALUE={LIMIT(V(N_P,MID), V(VEE,MID)+RSW, V(VCC,MID)-RSW)}
R_O N_O N_S R_NOISELESS 10
V_SENSE N_S OUT 0
* Current limit: beyond ILIM the sensed current pulls the pole node back.
G_LIM N_P MID TABLE {I(V_SENSE)} = (-1, -2000) ({-ILIM}, 0) ({ILIM}, 0) (1, 2000)
* Supply currents: the quiescent current and the output current from the rail that sources it.
G_Q VCC VEE VALUE={IQ}
G_SRC VCC 0 VALUE={IF(I(V_SENSE) > 0, I(V_SENSE), 0)}
G_SNK 0 VEE VALUE={IF(I(V_SENSE) < 0, -I(V_SENSE), 0)}
.MODEL R_NOISELESS RES (T_ABS=-273.15)
.MODEL C_UNIT CAP (C=1)
.ENDS BEHAVIOURAL_OPAMP
